<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Regular.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Bold.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<style>
  {%- comment -%} Real DIN Next LT Pro — brand font (Layer 1) {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "DINNextLTPro";
    src: url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Light.woff2' | asset_url }}") format("woff2"),
         url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Light.woff' | asset_url }}") format("woff");
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: "DINNextLTPro";
    src: url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Regular.woff2' | asset_url }}") format("woff2"),
         url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Regular.woff' | asset_url }}") format("woff");
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: "DINNextLTPro";
    src: url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Bold.woff2' | asset_url }}") format("woff2"),
         url("{{ 'DINNextLTPro-Bold.woff' | asset_url }}") format("woff");
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    D-DIN kept as fallback for any weight DIN Next lacks. The unicode-range keeps the
    browser from downloading it for characters it cannot draw anyway (an emoji in the
    announcement bar used to pull D-DIN Bold on every page).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "D-DIN";
    src: url("{{ 'D-DIN.woff2' | asset_url }}") format("woff2");
    unicode-range: U+0020-007E, U+00A0-00FF, U+0152-0153, U+2013-2014, U+2018-201D, U+2022, U+2026, U+20AC, U+2122;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: "D-DIN";
    src: url("{{ 'D-DIN-Bold.woff2' | asset_url }}") format("woff2");
    unicode-range: U+0020-007E, U+00A0-00FF, U+0152-0153, U+2013-2014, U+2018-201D, U+2022, U+2026, U+20AC, U+2122;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --font-body--family: "DINNextLTPro", "D-DIN", sans-serif;
    --font-subheading--family: "DINNextLTPro", "D-DIN", sans-serif;
    --font-heading--family: "DINNextLTPro", "D-DIN", sans-serif;
    --font-accent--family: "DINNextLTPro", "D-DIN", sans-serif;
    --font-primary--family: "DINNextLTPro", "D-DIN", sans-serif;
  }

  body {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
  }
</style>
